      "name": "CPIStall",
      "type": "OPT",
      "description": "On average, each warp of this workload spends 0.8 cycles being stalled waiting for the micro scheduler to select the warp to issue. Not selected warps are eligible warps that were not picked by the scheduler to issue that cycle as another warp was selected. A high number of not selected warps typically means you have sufficient warps to cover warp latencies and you may consider reducing the number of active warps to possibly increase cache coherence and data locality. This stall type represents about 32.4% of the total average of 2.6 cycles between issuing two instructions.",
